WEBVTT

00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,220
What are some other natural ways to reduce eye inflammation besides the

00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:18,100
rife? I've been doing the rife and it has helped.

00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:21,540
So one of the things that you want to look at, whatever you have, okay, I have

00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:25,140
eye inflammation. The first thing you want to ask your question,

00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:29,140
ask yourself and you probably already have is why?

00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:33,700
So why do I have eye inflammation? Was there an irritant?

00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:39,940
Did I, was I exposed to something? Is it a histamine type reaction in my eye?

00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:43,780
Meaning like an allergic reaction, we're at that time of year where,

00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:47,700
you know, that's a possibility where there's a lot of allergens in the air.

00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:55,380
Is it something else that I have used a cream on my face or something like that

00:00:55,380 --> 00:01:00,900
that could have been an irritant? So do ask that question and kind of put your

00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:04,660
Sherlock Holmes hat on and see if there was anything that caused that inflammation.

00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:16,020
There are some nutrients for eye issues that people have purchased on our store.

00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:25,620
I don't know the validity of all of those things. I know in the past that I remember,

00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:33,140
actually it was one of my first cancer patients ever way, way back in the early, in the late 90s

00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:43,780
that her friend came in with her and she had a blocked eye duct and they were going to actually,

00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:48,740
she was scheduled for surgery and she had a bunch of swelling around her eye and they were going to

00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:53,060
go in there. Actually, she was explaining to me the surgery that they have to literally go in there

00:01:53,060 --> 00:02:01,300
with a drill bit to drill that out. And this is what we did right in the office and I actually said,

00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:07,220
well, let's do the right one and let's see if that helps. And actually we did the right one and she

00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:13,220
came back with her friend the next visit, which I think was like two days later and she said it's

00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:18,980
all gone. She can't hold her surgery. I mean, just one treatment with the right made to open up to that

00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:25,700
duct. So if you have, you know, there's other causes to it, there's other issues that you can

00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:34,260
have with an eye that could be in infection. So if you have bacterial infection or viral infection,

00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:41,380
you might want to address that and address that with the right. So if you're running the right

00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:46,580
on just inflammation that will help with inflammation, but still not addressing the reason why,

00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:50,900
because the reason why a person could have inflammation is because of the virus or because of the

00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:58,900
bacteria. So you'd have to do a little investigation. I don't, I don't off the top of my head know

00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:07,300
the most common eye bacterial infections and what bacteria it is. But if you did Google that,

00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:13,700
just Google the most common bacterial eye infections or viral eye infections and then whatever

00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:18,660
that comes up in that Google search, you could just run that program on your right because most likely

00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:30,260
your right has that bacteria in the list, in the alphabetical list. If it's thought that it's

00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:36,820
a virus, then you could run the viral program as well. So there's just a viral complex program on the

00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:45,940
right that may be extremely helpful.

